{"name":"Encore Teal","hex":"#30525b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"encore","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brief extra performance, done after the main performance is complete.","A call or demand (as by continued applause) for a repeat performance."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Please perform again!"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encore"},{"term":"teal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small freshwater ducks of the genus Anas that are brightly coloured and have short necks.","A dark, somewhat bluish-green colour; a dark cyan."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a bluish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Encore","blocks":[{"text":"An encore is an additional performance given by performers at the conclusion of a show or concert, usually in response to extended applause from the audience. They are regarded as the most complimentary kind of applause for performers. Multiple encores are not uncommon, and they initially originated spontaneously, when audiences continued to applaud and demand additional performance from the artists after they had left the stage. However, in modern times they are rarely spontaneous and are usually a pre-planned part of the show."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Federspiel_Austrian_World_Music_Awards_2015_Encore_06.jpg/330px-Federspiel_Austrian_World_Music_Awards_2015_Encore_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encore","wikidata":"Q1363276"},{"title":"Teal","blocks":[{"text":"Teal is a dark cyan color. Its name comes from that of a bird, the Eurasian teal which has a similarly colored stripe on its head. The word is often used colloquially to refer to shades of cyan in general."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg/330px-Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teal","wikidata":"Q1078214"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Historic_ENCORE_%40_MET.JPG/500px-Historic_ENCORE_%40_MET.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Historic_ENCORE_%40_MET.JPG/1280px-Historic_ENCORE_%40_MET.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Historic_ENCORE_%40_MET.JPG/500px-Historic_ENCORE_%40_MET.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Operatic tenor Javier Camarena finishing a rare encore at the Metropolitan Opera in 2014. Encores are officially banned on the MET stage.[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHistoric_ENCORE_%40_MET.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/San_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_%2853351816983%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-San_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_%2853351816983%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/San_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_%2853351816983%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-San_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_%2853351816983%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASan_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_